    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required deriving an owner's `locality` from their city via a fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), returning `UNKNOWN` otherwise, and exposing it on the owner API response that the acceptance tests read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only, derived field) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` and a `locality(Owner)` default method backed by a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`), falling back to `\"UNKNOWN\"`. This mirrors the existing `membershipTier`/`membershipNumber` derivation pattern and is used by the `RespondWithOwner` function that both the GET and create responders rely on.\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: per the project's OfficeFloor conventions this is a derived response field, so it lives in the DTO mapping (the same place the other derived fields live) rather than needing a new pipeline step.",
